From 5cbd2f176d03da227eb63f51dcd2506caa3d346e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 01:59:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(ui): show an inverted machine axis in the viewport,
 setup sheet and NC header

The origin triad keeps its right-handed program-frame arrows and notes an
inverted axis of the shown setup's machine under its letter ("Machine X+
moves left (inverted axis)"). The setup sheet gets a MACHINE AXES section,
one line per inverted axis of the setup's own machine. The script's
machine global carries invertedAxes, and fanuc.cps / haas.cps (the only
posts that translate an inverted axis) write "(MACHINE X+ MOVES LEFT -
INVERTED AXIS)" after the program-name line. Standard machines: no new
line anywhere. One wording table (machine::inverted_motion /
inverted_axis_line) feeds the triad and the sheet.

Fixes #375

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
